---
source: crates/migrate/tests/it/main.rs
expression: report(&migration)
---
# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://devlanes.run/v1/schema.json
# Generated by `devlanes migrate` from package.json.
# Comments starting with "migrated from" are notes to review.
# migrated from package.json: script lint:all also runs processes in parallel; only dev is migrated
# migrated from package.json: services come from script dev: concurrently -k -n dev-,css,docs "pnpm:dev:*" "tailwindcss -w -i src/app.css" "mkdocs serve -a localhost:8000" "npm run storybook"
project: concurrently
services:
  dev-api:
    run_script: "package.json#dev:api"
  dev-web:
    run_script: "package.json#dev:web"
  # migrated from package.json: runs through `pnpm exec`, assuming tailwindcss is a package binary (node_modules is not installed); drop the prefix if it is a global program
  css:
    run: pnpm exec tailwindcss -w -i src/app.css
  # migrated from package.json: runs through `pnpm exec`, assuming mkdocs is a package binary (node_modules is not installed); drop the prefix if it is a global program
  # migrated from package.json: port 8000 is now the lane's port (${{ self.port }}, also in PORT), so lanes do not collide
  docs:
    run: pnpm exec mkdocs serve -a localhost:${{ self.port }}
  storybook:
    run_script: "package.json#storybook"

--- notes ---
package.json: script lint:all also runs processes in parallel; only dev is migrated
package.json: services come from script dev: concurrently -k -n dev-,css,docs "pnpm:dev:*" "tailwindcss -w -i src/app.css" "mkdocs serve -a localhost:8000" "npm run storybook"
package.json [css]: runs through `pnpm exec`, assuming tailwindcss is a package binary (node_modules is not installed); drop the prefix if it is a global program
package.json [docs]: runs through `pnpm exec`, assuming mkdocs is a package binary (node_modules is not installed); drop the prefix if it is a global program
package.json [docs]: port 8000 is now the lane's port (${{ self.port }}, also in PORT), so lanes do not collide
